er header ... becomes milliseconds' and 'a provider delay above that wins' (provider_delay_ms carried on the signal)","Case (f): 'Retry-After: 30 (beyond the 15 s cap): 1 call, the raw error propagates, no sleep'"],"finding":"The mechanism by which a Retry-After exceeding the 15 s cap (case (f): Retry-After:30) causes a single call with no sleep is not fully specified. Step 1 says `RetryBudget` is unchanged and its `defer` arises only when 'the next delay would pass the 15 s cap' computed from its own exponential `_floor_delay` (2-3 s first) — which is under 15 s on the first attempt. The `provider_delay_ms` carried on the `AtomicSignal` is consumed by the coordinator, not by `RetryBudget`, so nothing described feeds a 30 s Retry-After into the budget's cap decision. As written, the first attempt's floor delay is <15 s, so the budget would return `retry` (and sleep ~30 s) rather than `defer`, contradicting case (f)'s expected '1 call, no sleep'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3faf5e7b4a18f0eb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / step 2 (provider_delay_ms) and Testing case (f) / AC cases (e)-(f)","norm_id":"naa83cbbfddeea8e0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A 429 with Retry-After larger than the remaining budget must be refused without sleeping","The executor cannot tell which component compares provider_delay_ms against the 15 s cap"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define `TransientRetryBudget.attempt_retry(provider_delay_ms)` to (a) choose `delay = max(RetryBudget floor, provider_delay_ms)` and (b) if `cumulative_sleep + delay > 15000` ms, treat the plan as `defer` and raise `transient_cell[0]` without sleeping; document that provider_delay_ms is passed in from the AtomicSignal.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that a retried update does not double-apply a non-idempotent side effect (e.g. confirm a comment is posted exactly once across the retry), locking in the comments-after-update_issue ordering the idempotency claim relies on.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope asserts comments run after update_issue (dispatch_one.py:434-440) so a retry has not posted comments","Testing cases assert call counts/applied/sleep but no case exercises the comment-ordering invariant on retry","E5 checklist: 'Changed/deleted behaviors get corresponding modify/remove-test work' and failover idempotency"],"finding":"The plan's idempotency-on-retry claim — that a retried update 're-sends only set-style writes (reporter, parent, fields) and has not posted comments yet' because comments run after update_issue — is load-bearing for failover safety but has no test. Cases (a)-(c) assert transport call counts and applied outcomes but none verifies that a retry does not double-apply a non-idempotent side effect (e.g. a comment post).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f254c22f3badaeb42","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section cases (a)-(c); Scope paragraph 'a retry re-sends only set-style writes ... and has not posted comments yet'","norm_id":"ndde496d189c25c9b","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State where each transient retry attempt is surfaced to operators (a log line / metric / coordinator diagnostic), since the transient path appends no outcome.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: transient signal returned 'without appending an outcome'","diagnostic=f\"HTTP {code}\" is set on the signal but the plan does not state it is logged/metricized per retry attempt","T5b checklist: 'New failure points instrumented with a metric/log/trace/alert'"],"finding":"The transient retry mechanism records no per-attempt operator-visible signal: the plan says transient dispatch returns the signal 'without appending an outcome', so a 429/5xx that is retried (and succeeds) leaves no outcome record — the only evidence of retries is the recorded clock in tests. Operators cannot see that the pass silently retried a throttled write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0fcd70b62803ccaa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3, 'make_coordinator_dispatch(..., transient_cell=None)' — 'return the signal without appending an outcome'","norm_id":"n89a8c537e76d8193","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the transient_cell lifecycle across ops in one pass: is it per-op (cleared/reset) or pass-scoped, and confirm the budget raise always reflects the current op's exception, not a stale one.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'transient_budget_factory(cell, clock_factory) building a fresh TransientRetryBudget(...) per atomic op' — fresh budget but the SAME cell","Plan: TransientRetryBudget 'raises transient_cell[0]' on exhausted/defer","T9 checklist: 'Shared/mutable state mutated atomically ... no check-then-act TOCTOU'"],"finding":"The shared transient_cell (one-element list holding the escaping HTTPError) is created once per pass in run_migrated_reroute and passed both to make_coordinator_dispatch and to transient_budget_factory, so it is shared across all atomic ops in the pass. The plan does not state whether the cell is cleared between ops; a stale exception from an earlier transient op could be raised by a later op's budget if the later op's dispatch path does not overwrite cell[0] before the budget's exhaustion raise.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5fe7ee14aec965bf","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3, 'run_migrated_reroute